### ============================================================
### Akka Platform Deployed Environment - API Test Suite
### ============================================================
###
### All four services share a single hostname, differentiated
### by URI prefix. This keeps URLs clean and manageable.
###
### SETUP: Expose all services on the shared hostname
###
###   akka services expose statement-service \
###     --hostname banking-microapp.gcp-us-east1.akka.services \
###     --uri-prefix /stmt
###
###   akka services expose product-service \
###     --hostname banking-microapp.gcp-us-east1.akka.services \
###     --uri-prefix /prod
###
###   akka services expose analysis-service \
###     --hostname banking-microapp.gcp-us-east1.akka.services \
###     --uri-prefix /anls \
###     --enable-cors
###
###   akka services expose recommendation-service \
###     --hostname banking-microapp.gcp-us-east1.akka.services \
###     --uri-prefix /recs \
###     --enable-cors
###
### Verify routes with:
###   akka services list-routes
###
### Routing table:
###   /stmt/*  → statement-service       (foundation layer)
###   /prod/*  → product-service          (product catalog)
###   /anls/*  → analysis-service         (AI analysis, CORS enabled)
###   /recs/*  → recommendation-service   (user-facing, CORS enabled)
###
### --enable-cors is used for services called from a browser/mobile app.
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = https://banking-microapp.gcp-us-east1.akka.services
@accountId = acc-1001
@statementId = stmt-2025-12


################################################################
### 0. SEED DATA - Run These First!
### Seeds mock data into statement-service and product-service.
### Must complete before any other requests.
################################################################

### 0.1 Seed statement data (creates account acc-1001 with transactions)
POST {{baseUrl}}/stmt/accounts/seed
Content-Type: application/json

### 0.2 Seed product catalog (creates 4 default banking products)
POST {{baseUrl}}/prod/products/seed
Content-Type: application/json


################################################################
### 1. STATEMENT SERVICE (/stmt)
### Foundation layer - manages accounts, statements, transactions.
### No dependencies on other services.
################################################################

### 1.1 Get all statements for an account
GET {{baseUrl}}/stmt/accounts/{{accountId}}/statements

### 1.2 Get a specific statement with its transactions
GET {{baseUrl}}/stmt/accounts/{{accountId}}/statements/{{statementId}}

### 1.3 Get all transactions for an account (across all statements)
GET {{baseUrl}}/stmt/accounts/{{accountId}}/transactions

### 1.4 Get transactions within a date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/stmt/accounts/{{accountId}}/transactions?from=2025-01-01&to=2025-12-31

### 1.5 Add a new transaction to a statement
POST {{baseUrl}}/stmt/accounts/{{accountId}}/statements/{{statementId}}/transactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "txn-deployed-001",
  "date": "2025-02-15",
  "amount": 250.00,
  "merchant": "Cloud Services",
  "category": "Business"
}


################################################################
### 2. PRODUCT SERVICE (/prod)
### CRUD operations for banking products.
### Independent - no dependencies on other services.
################################################################

### 2.1 List all products
GET {{baseUrl}}/prod/products

### 2.2 Get a specific product by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/prod/products/travel_rewards_card

### 2.3 Create a custom product
POST {{baseUrl}}/prod/products/prod-custom-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "prod-custom-001",
  "name": "Custom Savings Account",
  "description": "High-yield savings for frequent savers",
  "annualRate": 4.5,
  "minBalance": 1000,
  "category": "Savings",
  "tags": ["savings", "high-yield"]
}

### 2.4 Update an existing product
PUT {{baseUrl}}/prod/products/prod-custom-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "prod-custom-001",
  "name": "Custom Savings Account Plus",
  "description": "Enhanced high-yield savings with bonus rewards",
  "annualRate": 5.0,
  "minBalance": 500,
  "category": "Savings",
  "tags": ["savings", "high-yield", "bonus"]
}

### 2.5 Delete a product
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/prod/products/prod-custom-001


################################################################
### 3. ANALYSIS SERVICE (/anls)
### AI-powered transaction analysis (heuristic or agent mode).
### Depends on: statement-service (fetches statement data internally)
################################################################

### 3.1 Run analysis on a statement
### Triggers heuristic or agent mode (configured in application.conf)
### Internally calls: statement-service GET /accounts/{id}/statements/{sid}
POST {{baseUrl}}/anls/accounts/{{accountId}}/analysis/run?statementId={{statementId}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 3.2 Get analysis summary (auto-runs analysis if not cached)
GET {{baseUrl}}/anls/accounts/{{accountId}}/analysis/summary?statementId={{statementId}}


################################################################
### 4. RECOMMENDATION SERVICE (/recs)
### Primary user-facing endpoint for the mobile app.
### Orchestrates the full service chain.
### Depends on: analysis-service → statement-service
################################################################

### 4.1 Get product recommendations
### Full call chain:
###   Client → recommendation-service
###     → analysis-service (GET /accounts/{id}/analysis/summary)
###       → statement-service (GET /accounts/{id}/statements/{sid})
GET {{baseUrl}}/recs/accounts/{{accountId}}/recommendations?statementId={{statementId}}


################################################################
### 5. CROSS-SERVICE FLOW DEMONSTRATIONS
### Test bottom-up: statements → analysis → recommendations
################################################################

### SCENARIO A: Full Recommendation Flow (3-tier cascade)
### Triggers the entire chain. Response includes product recommendations
### based on spending pattern analysis.
GET {{baseUrl}}/recs/accounts/{{accountId}}/recommendations?statementId={{statementId}}

### SCENARIO B: Direct Analysis Flow (2-tier)
### Tests analysis independently. Calls statement-service internally.
### Response includes categorized transactions and spending breakdown.
POST {{baseUrl}}/anls/accounts/{{accountId}}/analysis/run?statementId={{statementId}}

### SCENARIO C: Statement Foundation (no dependencies)
### The base layer - works completely independently.
### Response includes statement with transaction list.
GET {{baseUrl}}/stmt/accounts/{{accountId}}/statements/{{statementId}}


################################################################
### 6. DATA INTEGRITY CHECKS
### Run after seeding to verify the full stack is working.
################################################################

### 6.1 Verify statements exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/stmt/accounts/{{accountId}}/statements

### 6.2 Verify analysis was computed
GET {{baseUrl}}/anls/accounts/{{accountId}}/analysis/summary?statementId={{statementId}}

### 6.3 Verify recommendations were generated
GET {{baseUrl}}/recs/accounts/{{accountId}}/recommendations?statementId={{statementId}}

### 6.4 Verify product catalog is populated
GET {{baseUrl}}/prod/products


################################################################
### DEPLOYMENT & TESTING GUIDE
################################################################
###
### STEP-BY-STEP:
###
###   1. Deploy all 4 services to Akka Platform
###   2. Expose all services on the shared hostname (see SETUP above)
###   3. Verify routes: akka services list-routes
###   4. Update @baseUrl if your hostname differs
###   5. Run seed requests (Section 0) first
###   6. Test bottom-up: statements → products → analysis → recommendations
###   7. Run data integrity checks (Section 6) to verify everything
###
### SERVICE DISCOVERY (internal):
###   Backend-to-backend calls (analysis → statement, recommendation → analysis)
###   use Akka's internal HttpClientProvider. These calls do NOT go through
###   the public hostname or URI prefixes - they use internal service mesh routing.
###
### MINIMAL EXPOSURE (production):
###   For production, only expose what the frontend/mobile app needs:
###     akka services expose recommendation-service --hostname ... --uri-prefix /recs --enable-cors
###     akka services expose product-service --hostname ... --uri-prefix /prod --enable-cors
###   Internal services (statement, analysis) communicate via service discovery.
###
### CORS:
###   --enable-cors adds CORS response headers on the route.
###   Use it for any service called directly from a browser/mobile app.
###   Services with @Acl(principal = INTERNET) allow external traffic.
###
### TROUBLESHOOTING:
###   - 404: Service not exposed, wrong hostname, or wrong URI prefix
###   - 503: Service not yet running or still starting up
###   - Empty analysis results: Seed statement data first (Section 0.1)
###   - Empty product list: Seed product data first (Section 0.2)
###   - CORS errors in browser: Ensure --enable-cors was used when exposing
